  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Isoleucine -&nbsp; &nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/3cc93f6a-5491-4c28-9dec-6d9dd5f76262.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 141px;\" /></p><p>Isoleucine is a neutral amino acid.</p><p>Cysteine -&nbsp; &nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/3d7ddb52-aa19-4c81-b01a-47f09d08f5b7.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 133px;\" /></p><p>Cysteine is a sulphur containing amino acid. It contain thiol group.</p><p>Lysine -&nbsp;&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/b619639f-ce8a-4928-b36e-0bfec343c983.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 173px;\" /></p><p>Lysine is a basic amino acid.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Methionine -&nbsp;&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/96f0dd1f-8354-4045-b48b-2b0e3660f1eb.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 191px;\" /></p><p>Methionine is a sulphur containing amino acid contain thioether group.</p><p>Glutamic acid -&nbsp; &nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a859acbf-0e87-4db6-9b85-e541b83d20bd.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 185px;\" /></p><p>Glutamic acid is an acidic amino acid.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
